.TH QUARTERDECK 1 "March 2026" "quarterdeck 0.1.10" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
quarterdeck \- local orchestration board for coding agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quarterdeck
.RI [ --port " " number|auto ]
.RI [ --no-open ]
.RI [ command ]
.br
.B quarterdeck task
.RI " " list|create|update|link|unlink|start
.RI " " [ options ]
.br
.B quarterdeck hooks
.RI " " ingest|notify|codex-wrapper
.RI " " [ options ]
.br
.B quarterdeck mcp
.br
.B quarterdeck diagnostics
.RI " " list|status|doctor|capture|watch|record|mark
.RI " " [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B quarterdeck
starts the local Quarterdeck runtime server and serves the web UI.

When launched inside a git repository, it opens that repository's indexed workspace.
When launched outside git, it starts with no active workspace or falls back to the first indexed project.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --port <number|auto>
Bind to a specific local port or pick the first available port starting at 3500.
.TP
.B --no-open
Do not open the browser automatically.
.TP
.B --help, -h
Show help text and exit.
.TP
.B --version, -v
Show version and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B task|tasks
Manage Quarterdeck board tasks from the CLI.

Subcommands:
.br
.B list
.RI [ --project-path " " path ]
.RI [ --column " " backlog|in_progress|review ]
.br
.B create
.B --prompt
.RI " " text
.RI [ --project-path " " path ]
.RI [ --base-ref " " branch ]
.br
.B update
.B --task-id
.RI " " id
.RI [ --prompt " " text ]
.RI [ --project-path " " path ]
.RI [ --base-ref " " branch ]
.br
.B link
.B --task-id
.RI " " id
.B --linked-task-id
.RI " " id
.RI [ --project-path " " path ]
.br
.B unlink
.B --dependency-id
.RI " " id
.RI [ --project-path " " path ]
.br
.B start
.B --task-id
.RI " " id
.RI [ --project-path " " path ]

All task commands return JSON.

Use kebab-case flags only.

.TP
.B hooks
Runtime hook helpers used by agent adapters.

Subcommands:
.br
.B ingest
.RI [ payload ]
.B --event
.RI " " to_review|to_in_progress|activity
.RI [ --source " " source ]
.RI [ --activity-text " " text ]
.RI [ --tool-name " " name ]
.RI [ --final-message " " text ]
.RI [ --hook-event-name " " name ]
.RI [ --notification-type " " type ]
.RI [ --metadata-base64 " " base64 ]
.br
.B notify
same options as
.BR ingest ,
but best-effort.
.br
.B codex-wrapper
.B --real-binary
.RI " " path
.RI [ agentArgs... ]

.TP
.B mcp
Deprecated compatibility command. Prints a deprecation warning and exits.
.TP
.B diagnostics
Discover and inspect Quarterdeck's private local diagnostic flight recorder.

Subcommands:
.br
.B list
lists active and recently retained stopped, failed, or crashed runtime instances.
.br
.B status
shows recorder and journal health.
.br
.B doctor
runs read-only subsystem checks; use
.B --request-browser
for a fresh metadata-only browser snapshot.
.br
.B capture
writes a canonical local bundle containing a correlated JSONL timeline, findings, bounded snapshots, and a hashed manifest.
.br
.B watch
watches bounded records for a limited duration.
.br
.B record
starts, reports, or stops an automatically expiring deep-recording window.
.br
.B mark
adds a bounded timeline marker.

The lightweight metadata-only flight recorder starts automatically. Opening the Diagnostics panel is not required. Deep recording is explicit, scoped, capped at 15 minutes, and does not enable terminal transcripts or Git diffs. Bundles are private local directories and are never uploaded automatically.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start server on the default port:
.B quarterdeck
.TP
Start server without auto-opening a browser:
.B quarterdeck --no-open
.TP
Start server on a custom port:
.B quarterdeck --port 9000
.TP
List tasks for the current workspace:
.B quarterdeck task list
.TP
Create and start a task manually:
.B quarterdeck task create --prompt "Implement API pagination"
.TP
Ingest a hook event:
.B quarterdeck hooks ingest --event to_review
.TP
Capture current diagnostic evidence:
.B quarterdeck diagnostics capture --request-browser
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful execution.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR npm (1)
